{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink home-monitoring bundle connects my earlier door-alarm purchase with my recent Alexa devices, giving me a useful new capability to explore if installation fits my home.",
    "The Alexa-compatible doorbell and Echo Auto fit my interest in extending what my existing devices can do, although I would compare the doorbell with the bundle and check car and phone compatibility before choosing Echo Auto."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another Echo display, an older Dot, and a Fire TV Stick mostly repeat functions covered by my recent Show 5, fourth-generation Dot, and Stick 4K Max; familiarity alone does not create a current need.",
    "Buying external storage does not mean I need an internal SSD, especially without confirmed compatibility, and neither earbuds nor a headphone adapter addresses a need I currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest more Alexa devices even when they duplicate something I recently added.",
    "My history of buying computer accessories and storage seems to have been stretched into interest in accessories and upgrades without a specific task or compatibility match."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they can satisfy a need: adding a stand for my Show 5 suggests completing that setup, not immediately seeking another display.",
    "My accessory purchases often serve particular equipment or practical needs, such as replacement remote batteries; a useful next choice needs that concrete connection rather than a broad electronics resemblance."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognize my interest in Alexa and practical electronics, but miss the difference between adding a useful capability and duplicating equipment I already have."
}"}
